I am actually not too concerned about the filtering of the targets as we ran another CNV caller and with our particular data set (which contains some very large non-exonic regions) we were able to call most of the CNVs we were expecting with about 7000 targets passing the QC filters. My concern is the qcmat bit of code. I ended up commenting out that block as that is what another user who encountered the same problem suggested:

#qcmat=cbind(qcmat[,1:3],gene,qcmat[,4:12])
#colnames(qcmat)[4]='gene'
#qcmat[,1]=chr.all
#write.table(qcmat,file=paste(opt$outdir, projectname,'_qcmat','.txt',sep=''),sep='\t',quote=F,row.names=F)

I am currently running codex overnight and should be able to update with my results tomorrow.

